\pxi-2.6,l2.6;1. STIRRUP SPACING IS DIMENSIONED TO BAR CENTERLINES.\P2. REINFORCEMENT IS SHOWN REPRESENTATIVELY: THE FIRST AND LAST BAR OF EACH RUN ARE DRAWN.\P3. FOR SECTIONS A-A AND B-B AND PEDESTAL DETAILS, SEE SHEET B4-2. FOR SECTION C-C AND VIEW
  3
S D-D AND E-E, SEE SHEET B4-3. FOR SECTIONS F-F AND G-G AND DETAILS "A" AND "B", SEE SHEET B4-4.\P4. THE SOIL REINFORCEMENT ATTACHED TO THE BACKWALL SHALL BE DESIGNED BY A SPECIALTY ENGINEER FOR A SERVICE LOAD OF ___ K/FT AND A FACTORED LOAD OF ___ K
  3
/FT USING THE DESIGN CRITERIA FOR PERMANENT MSE WALLS. COST OF FURNISHING AND INSTALLING THE SOIL REINFORCEMENT IS CONSIDERED INCIDENTAL TO THE COST OF THE END BENT.\P5. FOR REINFORCING BAR LIST, SEE SHEET B4-11.\P6. PILE OFFSETS ARE FROM THE PGL, + 
  1
TO THE RIGHT LOOKING UP-STATION. CUTOFF ELEVATIONS ARE TO THE NEAREST 0.1 FT.\P7. MODEL CHECK (REMOVE BEFORE ISSUE): BACKWALL TOP AT CAP END END BENT 1 IS 47.192 IN THE CAD MODEL AND 47.132 IN THE SELECTED GEOMETRY CAD TABLES; RECONCILE BEFORE ISSUE.
